ys/news-etl@59cce39/content/data/versions/612.json", "paragraphs": ["Gavin Williams struck out 12 batters for Cleveland. José Ramírez hit a two-run homer. That was the only score in the game. The Guardians won 2-0.", "Cleveland lost the first two games of the series. Then they won three games in a row. Now they will play the Tampa Bay Rays on Monday.", "Cleveland pitchers struck out 21 batters in the game. That is a record for a nine-inning playoff game. The White Sox got only three hits.", "Williams also got the save in Game 4. He is the third pitcher in playoff history to do this. Cleveland has not won the World Series since 1948."], "paragraphs_zh": ["加文·威廉姆斯为克利夫兰队三振了12名击球手。何塞·拉米雷斯打出一记两分本垒打。这是比赛中唯一的得分。守护者队以2比0获胜。", "克利夫兰队输掉了系列赛的前两场比赛。然后他们连赢了三场。现在他们将在周一迎战坦帕湾光芒队。", "克利夫兰队的投手在这场比赛中三振了21名击球手。这是九局季后赛的纪录。白袜队只打出了三支安打。", "威廉姆斯在第四场比赛中也拿到了救援成功。他是季后赛历史上第三位做到这一点的投手。克利夫兰队自1948年以来就没有赢得过世界大赛。"], "body": "Gavin Williams struck out 12 batters for Cleveland. José Ramírez hit a two-run homer. That was the only score in the game. The Guardians won 2-0.\n\nCleveland lost the first two games of the series. Then they won three games in a row. Now they will play the Tampa Bay Rays on Monday.\n\nCleveland pitchers struck out 21 batters in the game. That is a record for a nine-inning playoff game. The White Sox got only three hits.\n\nWilliams also got the save in Game 4. He is the third pitcher in playoff history to do this. Cleveland has not won the World Series since 1948.", "body_zh": "加文·威廉姆斯为克利夫兰队三振了12名击球手。何塞·拉米雷斯打出一记两分本垒打。这是比赛中唯一的得分。守护者队以2比0获胜。\n\n克利夫兰队输掉了系列赛的前两场比赛。然后他们连赢了三场。现在他们将在周一迎战坦帕湾光芒队。\n\n克利夫兰队的投手在这场比赛中三振了21名击球手。这是九局季后赛的纪录。白袜队只打出了三支安打。\n\n威廉姆斯在第四场比赛中也拿到了救援成功。他是季后赛历史上第三位做到这一点的投手。克利夫兰队自1948年以来就没有赢得过世界大赛。", "text": "Gavin Williams struck out 12 batters for Cleveland. José Ramírez hit a two-run homer. That was the only score in the game. The Guardians won 2-0. Cleveland lost the first two games of the series. Then they won three games in a row. Now they will play the Tampa Bay Rays on Monday. Cleveland pitchers struck out 21 batters in the game. That is a record for a nine-inning playoff game. The White Sox got only three hits. Williams also got the save in Game 4. He is the third pitcher in playoff history to do this. Cleveland has not won the World Series since 1948.", "vocab": [{"word": "strike out", "pos": "verb", "zh": "三振出局", "note": "棒球术语，指投手让击球手出局", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "homer", "pos": "noun", "zh": "本垒打", "note": "也叫 home run，指击球手打出全垒打", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "series", "pos": "noun", "zh": "系列赛", "note": "指多场比赛组成的系列赛", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "playoff", "pos": "noun", "zh": "季后赛", "note": "指常规赛后的淘汰赛", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "save", "pos": "noun", "zh": "救援成功", "note": "棒球术语，指投手保住领先优势结束比赛", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "record", "pos": "noun", "zh": "纪录", "note": "指最佳成绩", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "hit", "pos": "noun", "zh": "安打", "note": "棒球术语，指击球手成功上垒", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "World Series", "pos": "noun", "zh": "世界大赛", "note": "美国职业棒球大联盟的总冠军赛", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Williams strikes out 12 as Guardians blank White Sox to complete ALDS comeback", "summary_original": "Williams fans 12 as Cleveland win decisive Game 5\nRamírez’s two-run homer provides only scoring\nGuardians to face Rays for place in World Series\nGavin Williams struck out 12, José Ramírez homered on a pitch just above home plate and the Cleveland Guardians beat the Chicago White Sox 2-0 on Saturday night to complete a comeback from a 2-0 deficit in their best-of-five American League Division Series.\nCleveland open the American League Championship Series at Tampa Bay on Monday night, seeking their first World Series appearance since 2016. The Guardians/Indians franchise have not won the title since 1948, the longest drought among MLB teams.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Williams strikes out 12 as Guardians blank White Sox to complete ALDS comeback\nWilliams fans 12 as Cleveland win decisive Game 5\nRamírez’s two-run homer provides only scoring\nGuardians to face Rays for place in World Series\nGavin Williams struck out 12, José Ramírez homered on a pitch just above home plate and the\nCleveland Guardians\nbeat the Chicago White Sox 2-0 on Saturday night to complete a comeback from a 2-0 deficit in their best-of-five American League Division Series.\nCleveland open the American League Championship Series at Tampa Bay on Monday night, seeking their first World Series appearance since 2016. The Guardians/Indians franchise have not won the title since 1948, the longest drought among\nMLB\nteams.\nGuardians pitchers struck out 21, the most in a nine-inning postseason game. The White Sox managed just three hits, putting only nine balls in play, and struck out 75 times over the series.\nTwo days after getting the save in Game 4, Williams became just the third pitcher in postseason history to get the last out of a game and start the following game when his team faced elimination in both.\nHe did not allow a hit until Kyle Teel looped a knuckle-curve into right field with two outs in the sixth, two innings after Ramírez homered for the second straight game, a two-run drive off Sean Burke.\nAfter a walk loaded the bases, Erik Sabrowski relieved Williams and struck out Munetaka Murakami.\nWilliams’s 12 strikeouts tied Cleveland’s record for a postseason game. He got 22 swings and misses, and his 24 strikeouts over three games tied for the second most in a best-of-five postseason series.\nHunter Gaddis followed Sabrowski and got four outs. Cade Smith finished for his first career five-out save, striking out the side in the ninth. He blew a fastball by Tristan Peters for the final out, setting off a celebration at Progressive Field.\nChicago, the first team to reach the playoffs after three straight 100-loss seasons, have not won the World Series since 2005.\nExplore more on these topics\nMLB\nCleveland Guardians\nChica